# Switch several digital outputs, addressed by their iRC panel numbers (e.g. DOut31), in the
# given order and back to back. The driver subtracts its dio_irc_offset (default 1: CRI "DOUT 30"
# switches iRC DOut31) and sends one "CMD DOUT <n> true|false" per entry.
#
# The request is validated completely before anything is sent: non-empty, equal lengths, every
# number in the driver's allowed set (parameter dio_allowed_outputs, default 21-27; the knife
# DOut31 is NOT allowed unless a deployment opts in, e.g. dio_allowed_outputs="21-27,31"), no
# duplicates. Any violation rejects the whole request and nothing is sent.
#
# success means the commands were SENT (as for SetDigitalOutput), not that the controller
# switched the outputs: confirm via the ~/digital_io topic (igus_rebel_msgs/DigitalIOState).
uint8[] irc_outputs   # iRC output numbers
bool[] states         # desired state per entry (same length as irc_outputs)
---
bool success
string message
